## Context
Finding (a) of the 0818 clone run (`verification/clone/0818-clone-rung-2026-09-23.json`):
the sitter ended with `failed` 391. Accounted for in
`verification/clone/0818-findings-2026-09-24.md` (probe
`verification/probes/clone_findings_0818.py`, output
`verification/clone/0818-findings-2026-09-24.json`):

- 367 `missing-source`: in-scope attachments whose file is not on disk in the
  pristine copy either: group files Zotero has not downloaded (sync state
  to-download), user-library rows at in-sync with no file, 3 dead linked paths.
  This is library state, counted as `failed` by design (ticket 0699).
- 24 `failed-session`: 23 already failed on doudou on 2026-09-06. 18 are
  real PDFs whose native-extraction error the sitter records only as the class
  `Error`; 6 are empty or HTML files labelled `application/pdf`.

Not a sitter defect, and not a live-install blocker. What stays open is why
native extraction rejects the 18 PDFs.

## Exit criteria
- [x] In a reflink arena on padme (Xvfb), `Zotero.SDT.ensure()` on `1/J2XJRQXE`
      with debug output on; the thrown message recorded in this log
- [x] The 18 PDFs classed from that message: native limit (0606's population)
      or something the sitter should handle
- [x] Decided, with the author: whether the byte sniff should class an empty or
      HTML file labelled PDF as `unsupported / mismatched-type`, as it already
      does for a zip, so those 6 stop reaching the worker every session
